   "evidence": "Assembly.lean:151-161 quantifies `c : \u2115+` with no link to `d.characteristic`; `Index.lean:539,542,555,560` provide `characteristic`, `characteristic_prime`, `fieldOrder_eq_characteristic_pow`, `fieldExponent_pos`, so the stronger statement is provable from the two explicit branch lemmas already in the file (Assembly.lean:130-143).",
   "file": "TauCeti/GroupTheory/SpecificGroups/CFSG/Datum/Assembly.lean",
   "fix": "Strengthen the conclusion to pin `c` to the characteristic, e.g. `\u2203 n k : \u2115, 0 < n \u2227 0 < k \u2227 d.datumSteinberg ^ n = RootPairingIsogeny.smulId _ \u27e8d.characteristic ^ k, pow_pos d.characteristic_prime.pos k\u27e9`. Both branches already supply it via `ValidLieTypeIndex.fieldOrder_eq_characteristic_pow` (Index.lean:555) and `fieldExponent_pos` (Index.lean:560): graph-twisted gives `c = q^e = p^(fieldExponent * e)`, half-Frobenius gives `c = q = p^fieldExponent`. Otherwise weaken the three docstring passages to say only 'some power is a scaling'.",
   "issue": "`exists_pow_datumSteinberg_eq_smulId` concludes only `\u2203 n c : \u2115+, 0 < n \u2227 \u03c3^n = smulId _ c` with `c` unconstrained. A scaling by an arbitrary positive integer is not a Frobenius, so the statement does not carry the Steinberg-endomorphism property the docstrings attribute to it: line 145-146 (\"the property that defines a Steinberg endomorphism: some power of it is a Frobenius\"), line 41-42 (\"That is the defining property of a Steinberg endomorphism in Steinberg's sense, and on the group layer it is the reason the fixed groups of milestone L3 are finite at all\"), and line 64-66 (\"the root-datum form of 'some power of a Steinberg endomorphism is a Frobenius'\"). A consumer needing 'some power is a Frobenius' cannot get it from this lemma.",
   "line": "151"
  }
 ],
